assistant: Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

Vendor version 2026-10-01 started paginating `/products` without updating its spec. It now returns only the first page plus a `next_cursor`. `search_products` read just that one response, so for "cable" it returned 5 of the 7 matches while still reporting `total: 7`. The handler now keeps requesting `/products?q=…&cursor=<next_cursor>` until `next_cursor` is null and combines all the pages. On 2026-01-01, `next_cursor` is already null, so it makes the same single request and the v1 fixtures produce the same output. Typecheck, lint and the other tests pass. The repro test now fails with UNMATCHED_REQUEST because the recording has no `&cursor=5` request, so it needs re-recording. Separately, the same recording shows 2026-10-01 prices in cents (6900 where v1 had 69), which breaks the `items.price.range` rule. I left that alone because this repro test doesn't cover it.

Subject: follow next_cursor when searching products

Vendor version 2026-10-01 started paginating `/products` without updating its spec. It now returns only the first page plus a `next_cursor`. `search_products` read just that one response, so for "cable" it returned 5 of the 7 matches while still reporting `total: 7`. The handler now keeps requesting `/products?q=…&cursor=<next_cursor>` until `next_cursor` is null and combines all the pages. On 2026-01-01, `next_cursor` is already null, so it makes the same single request and the v1 fixtures produce the same output. Typecheck, lint and the other tests pass. The repro test now fails with UNMATCHED_REQUEST because the recording has no `&cursor=5` request, so it needs re-recording. Separately, the same recording shows 2026-10-01 prices in cents (6900 where v1 had 69), which breaks the `items.price.range` rule. I left that alone because this repro test doesn't cover it.
